---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/lib/site";

// Linked from the footer and from Google's OAuth consent screen for the tools under
// ekkelenkamp.dev. Bump the date whenever the text changes.
const updated = { iso: "2026-11-04", label: "4 November 2026" };
const contact = site.email;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy · Guus Ekkelenkamp"
  description="What ekkelenkamp.dev and the tools under it collect, how it is used, and how to have it removed."
  mainClass="wrap"
>
  <article class="policy prose" aria-labelledby="policy-title">
    <h1 id="policy-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="policy__updated">
      Last updated: <time datetime={updated.iso}>{updated.label}</time>
    </p>

    <p>
      This policy covers ekkelenkamp.dev and the services Guus Ekkelenkamp runs under it, including sign-in
      via Google for access to personal tools.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The website itself sets no cookies and uses no analytics or third-party scripts. The web server keeps a
      short request log (time, page, status, referrer and browser type, without IP addresses) to keep the site
      running. Cloudflare delivers the site and processes your IP address to do so. If you turn the keyboard
      shortcuts off, that choice is stored in your own browser and never sent anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in with Google, we receive your name, email address and profile picture. This is used only
      to check whether you are allowed access. We do not request access to your Gmail, Drive, contacts or any
      other Google data.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is used and stored</h2>
    <p>
      Sign-in is handled by Cloudflare Access, which keeps a session cookie and an access log (email address,
      time, IP address) for security purposes. We do not sell, share or use this data for advertising or
      analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Access logs are kept according to Cloudflare’s standard retention. You can ask for your data to be
      removed at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or removal requests: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  @layer components {
    .policy {
      padding-block: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 5rem);
    }

    .policy h1,
    .policy h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 400;
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .policy h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-h1);
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .policy h2 {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      font-size: var(--text-h3);
    }

    .policy__updated {
      color: var(--ink-subtle);
      font-size: var(--text-small);
    }
  }
</style>
